items=[('Inherited matching','Species and hybrid song preferences support inherited sender–receiver matching, but do not identify a shared gene or channel.'),('Directional acoustics','Foreleg tympana combine external sound with tracheal inputs; contralateral-spiracle phase strongly contributes to forward directionality.'),('Input and selectivity','Thoracic and ascending cells can copy pulses without recognizing their rhythm; local brain processing creates more selective output.'),('Rebound and coincidence','LN5 generates intrinsic offset-linked rebound; delayed excitation combines with AN1 input in LN3, and LN4 integrates enhanced excitation with inhibition.'),('Recognition and steering','Selective recognition and fast directional corrections are distinct interacting processes; net phonotaxis can accumulate from steering toward individual pulses.'),('Evidence and limits','Proposed connections and molecular mechanisms require their own causal tests, and the five-neuron circuit does not explain all context-dependent pulse-duration responses.')]
tk={'items':[{'lead':a+'.','text':b} for a,b in items],'cite':'Hoy & Paul (1973); Michelsen et al. (1994); Hedwig & Poulet (2004); Schöneich et al. (2015); Zhang & Hedwig (2023)','refs':[x[1] for x in R.values()],'transcript':[a+'. '+b for a,b in items]}
